1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:19,254
A real job: an L-shaped kitchen for Mia Novak, with a pie-cut corner. Click New job.

2
00:00:19,254 --> 00:00:31,171
Add cabinets in walking order: the left wall first, from its front end to the corner.

3
00:00:31,171 --> 00:00:40,237
Then the corner: the Pie-cut corner base preset is 36" along each wall.

4
00:00:40,237 --> 00:00:57,598
Then the back wall, left to right: the 36" sink base, a 24" base and an 18" drawer base.

5
00:00:57,598 --> 00:01:00,563
Six cabinets, B1 to B6. B3 is the pie-cut corner.

6
00:01:00,563 --> 00:01:13,348
The room: 114" along the back wall, 108" down the left wall.

7
00:01:13,348 --> 00:01:22,179
Arrange puts the pie-cut in the back-left corner and runs the other cabinets out from both legs.

8
00:01:22,179 --> 00:01:25,180
The back run is exactly 114": 36 + 36 + 24 + 18. No gap, so no filler is needed.

9
00:01:25,180 --> 00:01:37,799
In 3D, the L wraps the corner with one continuous countertop line.

10
00:01:37,799 --> 00:01:44,959
Open the corner cabinet. Back on the Cabinets tab, click the pencil on B3.

11
00:01:44,959 --> 00:01:48,571
Both legs are 36" long and 24" deep. Each leg has its own door, hung on Salice hinges.

12
00:01:48,571 --> 00:01:51,153
Corner cleats are on: a small block under each L shelf's back corner, fixed on site.

13
00:01:51,153 --> 00:01:54,252
The 6" x 2" cleat size has a Configure badge until the shop confirms it.

14
00:01:54,252 --> 00:01:58,919
The parts table: bottom, top and shelf are L-shaped, banded on their inside edges L3 and W3.

15
00:01:58,919 --> 00:02:05,978
The corner cleat is a part of its own, cut from the carcass board with the job.

16
00:02:05,978 --> 00:02:14,171
The Cut list tab lists every part. The L parts carry their L3 / W3 banding.

17
00:02:14,171 --> 00:02:18,887
Near the end: Shelf 1 corner cleat, 6" x 2", one for B3.

18
00:02:18,887 --> 00:02:22,622
Nesting: the whole kitchen fits on six 5 x 12 ft sheets.

19
00:02:22,622 --> 00:02:30,467
Sheet 3 holds the L bottom and top. Each L takes its full rectangle on the sheet.

20
00:02:30,467 --> 00:02:33,643
The little part #41 next to them is the corner cleat.

21
00:02:33,643 --> 00:02:39,261
Labels come from the Output tab. Machine output switches stay off: this is a preview.

22
00:02:39,261 --> 00:02:42,476
The L bottom's label shows its L shape, the banded inside edges and its sheet.

23
00:02:42,476 --> 00:02:45,984
The cleat gets its own label too, marked to fix on site.

24
00:02:45,984 --> 00:02:48,987
Corner to labels in one job: next, a kitchen with a blind corner, fillers and end panels.
